      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1840 the Western and Atlantic Railroad chose Marietta as its hub, sparking a boom that lasted until the line shifted to Atlanta in 1842.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marietta%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Kennesaw House, originally the Fletcher House hotel, now hosts the Marietta History Center and the Gone with the Wind Museum in its historic halls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
